   460                              <1> ; IDIV does exactly that. It is done in 32 bits, so that -32768 / -1 (whose
   461                              <1> ; quotient, 32768, does not fit in 16) wraps as the spec says instead of
   462                              <1> ; faulting. Dividing by 0 skips the IDIV in an unchecked build (two cells of
   463                              <1> ; no meaning: a and its sign); the checked build stops with Z.
