  1179                              <1> ; waitk. At a console: a wait on the input handle for the time (EAX: 0
  1180                              <1> ; just looks, -1 is INFINITE), then ReadConsoleInputA for one event. A
  1181                              <1> ; timed wait (1 ms or more) sets the high-resolution timer once for the
  1182                              <1> ; whole time and waits for the input or the timer (WaitForMultipleObjects
  1183                              <1> ; on v_hin and v_htm, which follow each other); without the timer it is a
  1184                              <1> ; plain WaitForSingleObject, which starts again with its whole time after
  1185                              <1> ; each event passed over. Only key-down events count: their character,
  1186                              <1> ; or for the left and right arrow keys (virtual keys 25h and 27h, which
  1187                              <1> ; have none) ^B and ^F. Anything else is passed over.
  1188                              <1> ; Input that is not a console (a pipe or a file) is read a byte at a time
  1189                              <1> ; with ReadFile, and only by a wait that is not just a look (a look would
  1190                              <1> ; eat the input); at its end the interpreter exits.
